# Phase 15 probe — NOT a pinned production query, NOT run in this phase.
#
# Purpose: discover what predicates the dati.senato.it osr: ontology
# actually exposes on a ?senatore/?mandato resource beyond the ones
# tools/queries/senato_senatori.rq already asks for (nome, cognome, foto,
# cittaNascita, provinciaNascita, nazioneNascita, dataNascita, tipoMandato,
# inizio/fineMandato) — specifically, whether anything resembling an
# elected-collegio reference exists at all.
#
# Why this is needed before writing a real collegio-join query: v2 Phase 8
# hit the exact same problem on the Camera side — the obvious-looking
# `?collegio` variable in the original query turned out to be the wrong
# granularity (plurinominale, not uninominale), and the correct field
# (dcterms:spatial on the election resource) was only found by running a
# live predicate-enumeration query against the graph, not by guessing from
# the ontology's naming conventions. See docs/v2/03-linkage-report.md and
# CLAUDE.md's "Audit/verify before implementing" methodology note, which
# cites that exact episode.
#
# This phase (15) is read-only / offline-only by its own scope — it must
# not touch the network, so this query is a DESIGN artifact only. Running
# it is a deliberate, separate later step under the project's refetch
# protocol (a human- or phase-approved decision to query
# https://dati.senato.it/sparql), not something to run automatically.
#
# Run manually (when that later step is approved) via:
#   python3 -c "from tools.sparql_client import run_query; ..." — or
#   any SPARQL client — against https://dati.senato.it/sparql, then read
#   the ?p / sample ?o values back to identify the real collegio predicate
#   (if one exists at all — it may simply not, since Senato's electoral
#   system pre-2022 didn't use uninominale/plurinominale the same way
#   Camera's did in every legislature, and this graph may not track it per
#   senator regardless of what the ISTAT boundary layer separately knows).

PREFIX osr:  <http://dati.senato.it/osr/>
PREFIX foaf: <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/>

# Enumerate every distinct predicate used directly on a Senatore resource,
# for the current legislature's mandates, with one sample object value per
# predicate so a human can eyeball which one (if any) looks collegio-shaped.
SELECT ?predicate (SAMPLE(?value) AS ?sampleValue) (COUNT(?value) AS ?occurrences)
WHERE {
  ?senatore a osr:Senatore ;
            osr:mandato ?mandato .
  ?mandato osr:legislatura 19 .
  { ?senatore ?predicate ?value }
  UNION
  { ?mandato ?predicate ?value }
}
GROUP BY ?predicate
ORDER BY ?predicate
